Z||000011||banditbalz||08-21-2001||11:20 PM||||I run 15.4 on a stock 2.8 with a Holley scoop and K+N airfilter combo. Have a best of 15.2 with stock geared 4 speed. 172,000 kms on the original motor, 3rd clutch, third tranny...<P>_ <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/banditbalz/" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/banditbalz/</A> <P><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||12
Z||000012||GSXPete||08-22-2001||12:08 PM||||jay...what do u guys have done? stock motor?||||reg||1
Z||000013||Carrolles||08-22-2001||02:00 PM||||85SE 4spd v-6.  New Grooms 2.8L (now a 2.9L)long block.  I ported the intake and exhaust manifolds and basically cleaned and painted everything else while assembling the engine.  New harmonic damper, water pump, a/c compressor, plugs/wires, hoses, belts, ignition module (stock), clutch (stock Borg Warner OEM), axels, rear sway bar (JC Whitney Addco), etc.  Stock size (205-70R14 I believe) BF Goodrich T/A radials on stock allow 14" rims.<P>Basically it is a stock rebuild.<P>With my G-tech-Pro I've gotten 7.5 second 0 to 60 mph times, 15.2 second/ 90.1 mph quarter mile.  No hot rod but fun anyway.<P>This is my daily driver commuting 17 miles one way to work on twisty mountain roads.  I look forward to the ride every morning and afternoon.  It's a shame the fun has to be interrupted by work.<P>Welcome to the forum.<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000014||1FST2M6||08-22-2001||02:08 PM||||i ran 13.6@103 on my dry nitrous system... this new car is making more hp/tq with a wet system but haven't run it yet at the track...yet.<P>dyned at 279hp/312lbft stock engine. LOTS of nitrous.  <P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fsthydrantsig.jpg">         <BR>www.engineered.net||||reg||1
