Z||000019||lildevil||08-22-2001||07:02 PM||||With the stock power plant i don't think you'll go much faster than mid 14's and thats after a complete rebuild and lots of money. 13's are possible with nitrous and turbos. But a rebuild is a must. Maybe not with your low milage car.  You may want to look into an engine conversion for more performance. Jays Northstar is way impresive<BR>but i think he could tell you is alot of work and alil pricey. Another choice maybe the 3.8 Supercharged V-6 out of the POntaic GrandPrix GTP. I have on in my car...spent less then 4000 dollars putting it in. Could be done for way less but i bought a 5000 mile motor and trans for 2500 dollars.  ANyways...I have gotten a 13.3 out of it so far on a humid and warm day. Can't wait til November.  Also i still get 30 miles to the gallon. And its easy to install.<P><P>------------------<BR>Earl Sessions<BR>1985 Fiero w/ 1998 Supercharged 3.8 V-6<BR>Best ET: 13.311 @100.75 mph<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/water3quarterthumb.jpg"> ||||reg||1
