Z||000022||Jay||08-22-2001||09:51 PM||||No I'm already married and my wife loves cars too.  (She's got a Suzuki Grand Vitara all done up!)  I'm ready to try something a little more exotic.  I've always loved Ferrari and I've always said I would own one.  Well, selling the N* would finance a nicely used 308/328.  Actually anything Italian will do, like a Maserati bi-turbo or Lamborghini Jalpa.<BR>  I've also always wanted to do up a rice rocket.  Yup, a Mitsubishi Eclipse AWD Turbo Spyder would do it.  So right now it looks like I may be looking for a Ferrari or Eclipse.  The only problem is they don't sell  Mitsubishi in Canada so I'd have to import one.  Know where I could find one cheap?<P>Last year I turned down a 308GT4 Ferrari for $18 000 Canadian because the N* wasn't ready to drive yet and I had my money tied up in that.  Now it's gone and I'm kicking myself.  Oh well, there is always this winter.  If I don't get the Ferrari or Eclipse than I'll change the N* to manual and sink more money into it instead of an Italian.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
